==============================================================================
  Metasploit Windows XP Exploit Modules - Complete Ranked List
==============================================================================

XP SP3 English (no patches) is the ideal target.  Meterpreter requires SP2+ on
modern MSF (v6+).  For SP0/SP1, use windows/shell/reverse_tcp instead.

Default open ports: 445 (SMB), 139 (NetBIOS), 135 (DCOM/RPC)
Optional: 3389 (RDP), 80 (IIS)

---

  S-TIER: LEGENDARY (remote, no creds, instant SYSTEM)

  1.  exploit/windows/smb/ms17_010_eternalblue         10/10
      NSA leak.  Kernel ring-0 via pool grooming.
      Port 445.  Works on XP SP0-SP3.
      Used by WannaCry.  The most devastating public exploit ever.

  2.  exploit/windows/smb/ms08_067_netapi               10/10
      Stack buffer overflow in Server service.
      Port 445/139.  72 targets across all SPs/languages.
      NX bypass on SP2/SP3.  The one everyone learns on.

  3.  exploit/windows/smb/smb_doublepulsar_rce           9/10
      The other half of the NSA toolkit.
      Injects a backdoor into SMB itself.  Very meta.

  4.  exploit/windows/smb/ms09_050_smb2_negotiate       8/10
      SMBv2 function table dereference.
      Elegant protocol negotiation exploit.

  5.  exploit/windows/dcerpc/ms03_026_dcom               7/10
      The Blaster worm vector.  Port 135.
      Vintage 2003.  Historic significance.

  6.  exploit/windows/smb/ms06_040_netapi                6/10
      Predecessor to MS08-067.  Same NetAPI32.dll.
      Want to see where MS08-067 evolved from? Run this first.

  7.  exploit/windows/smb/ms05_039_pnp                   5/10
      Plug and Play service overflow.  Clean SEH-based.

  8.  exploit/windows/smb/ms04_011_lsass                 5/10
      LSASS overflow.  Sasser worm.
      Need to run it twice on XP.

  9.  exploit/windows/smb/ms04_031_netdde                4/10
      NetDDE service.  Obscure protocol.

  10. exploit/windows/smb/ms09_001_write                 4/10
      SMB WriteAndX.  Simple but reliable.

